Subject: [PATCH] Wire --no-compress flag into --output-dot / --output-json

The --no-compress flag is declared in src/Main/Mode/Batch.hs with help text
"Do not use compressed sequent visualization", but the trace-output path
(outputTraces) ignores it: it hard-codes `defaultGraphOptions`, which has
`_goCompress = True`. As a result,

    tamarin-prover --prove --output-dot=FILE --no-compress in.spthy

produces output byte-identical to running without the flag.

This patch threads the existing flag into the GraphOptions used for both
--output-dot and --output-json, so the documented behaviour matches reality.

Why this matters for redx: compression is described in
lib/theory/src/Theory/Constraint/System/Graph/Simplification.hs as
"Unsound compression of the sequent that drops fully connected learns and
knows nodes". `compressSystem` can hide intruder KU action nodes whose
deduced term is a pair / inverse / public / nat (`hideAction`) and ISend /
IRecv / Coerce / Fresh nodes (`hideRule`). These are precisely the steps a
reconstructed attacker recipe needs to see. With this patch and the
existing --no-compress flag, redx's recipe extractor sees the uncompressed
trace.

This patch applies cleanly to both vendors/tamarin-prover/ and
vendors/tamarin-unchained/ since they share an identical Batch.hs.

---
 src/Main/Mode/Batch.hs | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/Main/Mode/Batch.hs b/src/Main/Mode/Batch.hs
--- a/src/Main/Mode/Batch.hs
+++ b/src/Main/Mode/Batch.hs
@@ -251,6 +251,8 @@
         outputTraces :: ClosedTheory -> IO ()
         outputTraces thy = do
             let graphOptions = defaultGraphOptions
+                  { _goCompress = not (argExists "noCompress" as)
+                  }
                 dotOptions = defaultDotOptions
                 serializeDot (label, system) = D.showDot label $ dotSystemCompact graphOptions dotOptions system
                 serializeJSON = sequentsToJSONPretty graphOptions
